Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:32:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable BIND_NOW by default

Enable immediate symbol binding for ELF executables and shared libraries using the existing internal and external linker support. Preserve -bindnow=false as an opt-out and extend ELF flag and RELRO coverage.

Fixes microsoft/go#851.
---
 src/cmd/link/doc.go                  |   2 +-
 src/cmd/link/internal/ld/elf_test.go | 125 +++++++++++++++++----------
 src/cmd/link/internal/ld/lib.go      |   2 +-
 src/cmd/link/internal/ld/main.go     |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cmd/link/doc.go b/src/cmd/link/doc.go
index b7857cfc177785179de83d241635524402dbce62..eba4299623b295f074c906b6549d2558329fa794 100644
--- a/src/cmd/link/doc.go
+++ b/src/cmd/link/doc.go
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ Flags:
 	-aslr
 		Enable ASLR for buildmode=c-shared on windows (default true).
 	-bindnow
-		Mark a dynamically linked ELF object for immediate function binding (default false).
+		Mark a dynamically linked ELF object for immediate function binding (default true).
 	-buildid id
 		Record id as Go toolchain build id.
 	-buildmode mode
